WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:05.635
Cedric's chair was placed at the opposite end of the table from the earl's.

2
00:00:05.636 --> 00:00:10.835
"This is a big chair," Cedric said, patting the arms.

3
00:00:10.836 --> 00:00:19.880
"Everything I've seen in this castle is huge—the furniture, the rooms. Even your dog!"

4
00:00:19.881 --> 00:00:26.854
"And does that bother you?" the earl asked, picking up a soup spoon.

5
00:00:26.855 --> 00:00:31.507
"Don't worry about me. I'll get used to it."

6
00:00:31.508 --> 00:00:36.032
Cedric looked down the long table.

7
00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:41.737
He was dazzled by the gleaming glasses, china, and silverware.

8
00:00:41.738 --> 00:00:45.576
Once again the earl had some positive thoughts about Cedric.

9
00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:50.922
"When the boy committed himself to helping me, he didn't give up.

10
00:00:50.923 --> 00:00:54.448
Even when it was clearly too much for him.

11
00:00:54.449 --> 00:01:00.420
And now he's refusing to admit that he's overwhelmed."

12
00:01:00.421 --> 00:01:07.885
"I hate to mention this," Cedric said. "But I notice you're not wearing your coronet."

13
00:01:07.886 --> 00:01:15.373
"No, it's only for special occasions like a coronation of a king or queen."

14
00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:21.220
"Mr. Hobbs thought an earl always wore a coronet," Cedric said.

15
00:01:21.221 --> 00:01:26.639
"But I thought you must take it off sometimes to put on your hat."

16
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:35.572
"That's right." His grandfather almost smiled. "I don't often wear it."

17
00:01:35.573 --> 00:01:39.473
The earl turned to the footman standing nearby.

18
00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:43.702
"Please tell the cook that the soup is delicious."

19
00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:47.293
The footman raised his eyebrows in surprise.

20
00:01:47.294 --> 00:01:54.708
If the earl had a message for the cook, it was usually a complaint.

21
00:01:54.709 --> 00:01:58.326
Cedric finished eating and leaned back in his chair.

22
00:01:58.327 --> 00:02:01.311
"You must be proud of this house.

23
00:02:01.312 --> 00:02:05.869
I'm only nine, so I haven't been to a lot of places.

24
00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:11.368
But this is the most beautiful house I've ever seen."

25
00:02:11.369 --> 00:02:18.441
"And you think I should be proud of it?" The earl took a sip from his water glass.

26
00:02:18.442 --> 00:02:21.525
"I'd be proud if it were my house.

27
00:02:21.526 --> 00:02:27.258
Everything about it is beautiful, including the trees in the park."

28
00:02:27.259 --> 00:02:31.083
Cedric paused and looked at the earl uncertainly.

29
00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:38.345
"It's a very big house for just two people to live in," Cedric went on.

30
00:02:38.346 --> 00:02:43.697
"If two people lived here and they weren't good friends . . ."

31
00:02:43.698 --> 00:02:51.395
He hesitated and played with his napkin. "They might feel lonely sometimes."

32
00:02:51.396 --> 00:02:56.483
"Do you think we'll be good friends?"

33
00:02:56.484 --> 00:03:01.889
"I think so," Cedric replied. "Mr. Hobbs and I were great friends.

34
00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.051
He was the best friend I had except my mother."

35
00:03:05.052 --> 00:03:10.631
Cedric was trying not to think of her, but that was impossible.

36
00:03:10.632 --> 00:03:14.958
This was the first night they'd ever been apart. The

37
00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:19.374
more he thought about his mother, the quieter he became. Even

38
00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:23.964
the earl noticed that he looked tired and sad. "Come

39
00:03:23.965 --> 00:03:29.863
here, Cedric, and help me back to the library." This

40
00:03:29.864 --> 00:03:35.614
time the earl did not lean so heavily on Cedric's shoulder. Cedric

41
00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:40.242
sat on the hearth rug near Dougal. For

42
00:03:40.243 --> 00:03:44.534
a few minutes, he stroked the dog's ears and looked at the fire. Once

43
00:03:44.535 --> 00:03:51.121
or twice he gave a sigh. "What

44
00:03:51.122 --> 00:03:55.815
are you thinking about?" the earl asked. "I

45
00:03:55.816 --> 00:04:05.813
was thinking about my mother . . . and . . . and . . . I need to walk around the room." The

46
00:04:05.814 --> 00:04:13.755
earl watched as Cedric worked to control his emotions. Dougal

47
00:04:13.756 --> 00:04:18.680
followed the boy, and Cedric laid a hand on his head. "He's

48
00:04:18.681 --> 00:04:25.966
a very nice dog," Cedric said. "I think he knows how I feel." "And

49
00:04:25.967 --> 00:04:28.942
how do you feel?" The

50
00:04:28.943 --> 00:04:33.909
earl didn't like watching his grandson struggle with homesickness. But

51
00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.872
he was proud that Cedric was making an effort to cope. When

52
00:04:37.873 --> 00:04:44.049
Cedric didn't reply, the earl said, "Come here." Cedric

53
00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:52.867
stepped closer. "Staying all night in another person's castle feels strange," he said. "Mama

54
00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.973
told me to remember that she isn't far away. And

55
00:04:56.974 --> 00:05:01.050
I can always look at the picture she gave me." Cedric

56
00:05:01.051 --> 00:05:08.048
leaned against the arm of the earl's chair and against the old man's arm too. He

57
00:05:08.049 --> 00:05:12.032
pulled a velvet-covered case from his pocket. "You

58
00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:17.548
press this button, and it opens, and there she is!" He

59
00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:20.505
looked up at the earl with a smile. "I

60
00:05:20.506 --> 00:05:25.409
don't want to see a picture of that woman!" the earl thought. But

61
00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:32.415
he looked anyway. He was surprised at how young and pretty she was. "I

62
00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:38.086
suppose you think you're fond of her," the earl said. "Oh,

63
00:05:38.087 --> 00:05:45.474
yes," Cedric replied. "We always tell each other everything .

64
00:05:45.475 --> 00:05:51.771
When I'm grown up, I'm going to work and take care of her."

65
00:05:51.772 --> 00:06:00.170
"What kind of job do you think you'll have?" the earl asked, even though he knew his heir would never work.

66
00:06:00.171 --> 00:06:07.559
"I'm not really sure," Cedric said. "Maybe I'll be a grocer like Mr. Hobbs."

67
00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:13.082
The earl's eyes widened in horror.

68
00:06:13.083 --> 00:06:17.237
Half an hour later, Mr. Havisham entered the library.

69
00:06:17.238 --> 00:06:21.426
Before he could speak, the earl hushed him.

70
00:06:21.427 --> 00:06:28.868
Cedric and Dougal were fast asleep in front of the fire.

